This is an aggregate. Each row's licence follows its source and is given per
row by the view `reception_licensed` (data/reception.sqlite), from
data/licenses.tsv. Rows under someone else's licence keep it: the licence in
section 2 covers this project's own work, not theirs.

1. PUBLIC DOMAIN — NOT CLAIMED

Public-domain source texts reproduced here are not claimed. A faithful
transcription of a public-domain text creates no new copyright, and none is
asserted. Anyone may take the source text and do anything with it. That
covers JFB, Matthew Henry, Barnes, Calvin, the Catena aurea in the Oxford
translation, and Wesley's Explanatory Notes. Rows from JFB, Henry, Barnes
and Calvin store locations only.

