This project's original work is licensed under the Creative Commons
Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 International License (CC BY-NC 4.0):

  (a) the structured data — its selection, arrangement, encoding,
      identifiers, verse keys and their normalization, the overlap columns,
      and the RCL normalization;
  (b) the in-house English of the Glossa ordinaria (source: glossa-ordinaria
      rows, from migne.app);
  (c) the code and build scripts.

Legal code: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/legalcode

Training machine-learning models on this material is expressly permitted,
including for commercial models.

3. THIRD-PARTY MATERIAL

- catena: CC BY-SA 4.0, from Catena's open-data layer. Those rows stay under
  CC BY-SA, not section 2. BY-SA and BY-NC material cannot be combined
  into one adapted dataset, so export them as separate files.
- barth-cd: pointers only. The Church Dogmatics is in copyright, and no
  words are stored.

